const course = {"id":"gia2plus","label":"A2+","source":"https://highlights.macmillan.com.ar/samples/secondary/getinvolved/A2plus/GetInvolvedA2plus_Scope_and_Sequence.pdf","starter":[{"title":"Let’s get personal!","source":"Student’s Book · pp. 8–9","words":[["school subject","школьный предмет"],["city centre","центр города"],["get dressed","одеваться"],["have a shower","принимать душ"],["take the bus","ехать на автобусе"],["after school","после школы"]],"grammar":{"title":"Wh- questions","rule":"Вопросительное слово ставим перед do/does или формой be.","items":[["Where ___ Maya live?","does","do,is"],["What ___ your favourite subject?","is","do,does"],["When ___ you go to the library?","do","are,does"],["___ does Theo travel to school?","How","Who,Whose"]]},"writing":"Write six lines about your school and a typical weekday. Include two questions to ask a new classmate."},{"title":"A world of languages","source":"Student’s Book · p. 10","words":[["France","Франция"],["French","французский"],["Brazil","Бразилия"],["Portuguese","португальский"],["Japan","Япония"],["Japanese","японский"]],"grammar":{"title":"There is / are and object pronouns","rule":"There is + единственное число, there are + множественное. После глагола используем me, him, her, it, us, them.","items":[["There ___ three language classes.","are","is,be"],["I know Maya. I play tennis with ___.","her","she,he"],["There ___ a map on the wall.","is","are,were"],["I like those books. I read ___ at home.","them","they,it"]]},"writing":"Introduce an imaginary exchange student. Mention their country, language and a question for the class."},{"title":"Starter round-up","source":"Student’s Book · pp. 6–11","words":[["favourite","любимый"],["introduce","представлять"],["speak","говорить"],["hobby","увлечение"],["school","школа"],["neighbourhood","район"]],"grammar":{"title":"Starter review","rule":"При повторении проверяй подлежащее, порядок слов и форму следующего глагола.","items":[["My sister ___ got a pet.","has","have,is"],["I enjoy ___ photos.","taking","take,took"],["___ do you live?","Where","Who,Whose"],["I speak to ___ every day. (Leo)","him","he,his"]]},"writing":"Write a short introduction for an exchange club. Include where you live, a language and two interests."}],"units":[{"title":"Stories","topic":"Жанры кино и игр, привычки у экрана","page":12,"words":[["comedy","комедия"],["documentary","документальный фильм"],["thriller","триллер"],["animation","анимация"],["ending","концовка"],["character","персонаж"],["be keen on","увлекаться"],["be interested in","интересоваться"],["be good at","хорошо уметь"],["be tired of","устать от"],["be afraid of","бояться"],["be excited about","быть в восторге от"]],"grammar":[{"title":"Present simple и частотность","rule":"С привычками используем present simple. Usually ставим перед смысловым глаголом, но после be.","items":[["Mia usually ___ a comedy on Friday.","watches","watch,is watching"],["I ___ play games after midnight.","never","am never,do never"],["How often ___ Leo watch documentaries?","does","do,is"],["Mia ___ often tired after a long film.","is","does,has"]]},{"title":"Present simple и present continuous","rule":"Present simple описывает привычки, present continuous — действие сейчас или временную ситуацию.","items":[["What ___ you watching right now?","are","do,is"],["I usually ___ games at weekends.","play","am playing,plays"],["Leo ___ a film at the moment.","is editing","edits,edit"],["Today we ___ on a short animation.","are working","works,work every week"]]}],"text":"Two friends planned a film night, but they disagreed about what to watch. Iris usually chooses comedies because she wants to relax after school. Ben prefers documentaries and suggested a film about a team of young inventors. They watched the trailer together and noticed that it was also funny. After the film they wrote short reviews. Both liked the characters, but Iris thought the ending was too quick. Now they are making a one-minute trailer for their own story.","reading":[["Why does Iris usually choose comedies?","She wants to relax.","She wants to learn history.","She dislikes all documentaries."],["What are the friends making now?","A one-minute trailer.","A long documentary.","A new review."]],"dialog":[["Maya","Are you free on Friday? The film club is showing a comedy at six."],["Theo","Yes, but I am helping with the animation workshop until five thirty."],["Maya","Good. Let's meet at the cinema entrance at a quarter to six."],["Theo","Perfect. I'll bring my review of last week's thriller."]],"listening":[["Where will they meet?","At the cinema entrance.","In the animation workshop.","At school."],["What time will they meet?","5:45.","5:30.","6:00."]],"speaking":"Recommend a film, game or book to a partner. Explain what makes its story interesting.","writing":"Write an 80-word review. Give a short plot summary, explain your opinion and say who might enjoy it.","contexts":["We wanted to laugh, so we chose a ___.","The film used real interviews and archive footage. It was a ___.","The detective was followed through the city in this ___.","The team used drawings that moved on screen to make an ___.","The final scene changed everything. Nobody expected that ___.","The girl who solves the mystery is my favourite ___.","I'm starting a film club for students who might ___ mysteries.","Would you ___ how directors plan action scenes?","Lea practises every day and hopes to ___ creating special effects.","After watching three trailers for the same film, you might ___ hearing about it.","I don't think you'd enjoy that horror film if you ___ spiders.","The performers can't wait to show their work. They must ___ the screening."],"extendedDialog":[["Maya","Are you free on Friday? The film club is showing a comedy at six."],["Theo","Yes, but I am helping with the animation workshop until five thirty."],["Maya","Good. Let's meet at the cinema entrance at a quarter to six."],["Theo","Perfect. I'll bring my review of last week's thriller."],["Maya","One more thing. My brother is coming for the first time, but he doesn't think comedies have much of a story. Can we show him the trailer?"],["Theo","Yes. Don't tell him the ending, though. I thought the film was about a lost animal, but the trailer only showed the first scene. The animal actually helps two people become friends."],["Maya","That sounds better than the usual joke after joke. Does the club still ask everyone to write a review?"],["Theo","Only once a month now. This week we're choosing the opening scene for our own film. I want it to start with a sound before we see anything."]],"extendedListening":[["What are they arranging and discussing?","A film-club visit and ideas for a new film.","A competition to finish the longest review.","A visit to an animal centre."],["Where will they meet?","At the cinema entrance.","In the animation workshop.","At school."],["What time will they meet?","5:45.","5:30.","6:00."],["Why might the brother hesitate?","He thinks comedies lack a good story.","He has already seen the film.","He dislikes going out on Fridays."],["How often do members write reviews now?","Once a month.","Every week.","Only at the end of the year."],["What idea does Theo suggest for the opening?","Let the audience hear something first.","Begin with the ending.","Show the two friends immediately."]],"dialogueWords":153,"readingLesson":{"title":"A trailer with a surprise","paragraphs":["Two friends planned a film night, but they disagreed about what to watch. Iris usually chooses comedies because she wants to relax after school. Ben prefers documentaries and suggested a film about a team of young inventors. They watched the trailer together and noticed that it was also funny. After the film they wrote short reviews. Both liked the characters, but Iris thought the ending was too quick. Now they are making a one-minute trailer for their own story.","At their next meeting, Iris brought a short **review** that described the film without giving away the ending. Ben brought a **storyboard** with six small drawings. He had drawn a chase in the last box, but Iris pointed out that the scene would take a long time to film safely. They decided to suggest movement with a series of close-up shots instead.","Their greatest **challenge** was sound. They tried recording in the playground, but the wind was louder than either actor. The school librarian offered them a quiet room after classes. There, they could read each line twice and **replace** any recording that was hard to hear. When four classmates watched the finished trailer, three could explain who the main character was, but none could guess the ending. The team was pleased. They wanted to give the **audience** just enough information to make it curious."],"trueFalse":[["F","Ben’s storyboard had twelve drawings.","It had six drawings."],["T","The wind made the voices difficult to hear.","The wind was louder than the actors."],["F","The librarian offered them a room before classes.","They could use the room after classes."],["T","None of the classmates guessed the ending.","All four were unable to guess it."]],"gaps":[["The storyboard had ___ small drawings.",["six","6"]],["They used a quiet room offered by the ___.",["librarian","school librarian"]],["___ classmates could explain who the main character was.",["three","3"]]],"definitions":[["review","a text that gives an opinion about something"],["storyboard","a series of drawings that plans what a film will show"],["challenge","a task or problem that is difficult to deal with"],["replace","to put something new in the place of something old"],["audience","the people who watch or listen to a performance"]]}},{"title":"Then and now","topic":"Предметы прошлого и события жизни","page":24,"words":[["typewriter","печатная машинка"],["record player","проигрыватель"],["camera","фотоаппарат"],["telephone","телефон"],["radio","радиоприёмник"],["washing machine","стиральная машина"],["move house","переезжать"],["start school","пойти в школу"],["leave school","закончить школу"],["get a job","устроиться на работу"],["grow up","расти"],["retire","выйти на пенсию"]],"grammar":[{"title":"Was, were и could","rule":"Was употребляем с I, he, she, it. Were — с you, we, they. После could глагол без to.","items":[["There ___ two radios in the shop.","were","was,are"],["My grandmother ___ read when she was five.","could","can,could to"],["There ___ a typewriter on the desk.","was","were,be"],["What ___ the cameras like?","were","was,did"]]},{"title":"Past simple и used to","rule":"Past simple рассказывает о событии в прошлом. Used to + глагол описывает прежнюю привычку или состояние.","items":[["They ___ house in 2019.","moved","move,used to move every day"],["My uncle ___ use a record player when he was young.","used to","uses to,is used to"],["Did you ___ school in this town?","start","started,starting"],["We didn't ___ to have a computer at home.","use","used,using"]]}],"text":"When Rosa helped to clear an old room, she found a small camera and a box of photos. Her grandfather explained that he used to take photographs on family trips. The camera could only take a limited number of pictures before he needed a new roll of film. Rosa noticed that some photos showed a tram outside her house. Today there is no tram on the street, but the old stop is still there. She compared the pictures with a modern map for a school project.","reading":[["What did Rosa use in her project?","Old photos and a modern map.","A record player and a radio.","Only a new camera."],["What is still on the street?","The old tram stop.","A working tram.","The old camera shop."]],"dialog":[["Maya","Did you find anything for the museum display?"],["Theo","Yes. My aunt gave me a record player from the nineteen eighties."],["Maya","Does it still work?"],["Theo","It does, but we need a cable. I'll bring it on Thursday, not Tuesday."]],"listening":[["What did Theo find?","A record player.","A radio.","A typewriter."],["When will he bring it?","Thursday.","Tuesday.","Friday."]],"speaking":"Choose one old object and explain how an earlier generation used it.","writing":"Write a short museum label for an old object. Include its date or period, its purpose and one difference from today.","contexts":["Before computers, she wrote her letters on a ___.","Dad keeps vinyl records beside his ___.","Bring a ___ if you want to take photos at the fair.","Our family used a ___ with a long wire to call people.","He turned on the ___ to hear the match score.","The ___ cleans clothes while we do other jobs.","We need to ___ because this flat is too small.","My cousin will ___ for the first time in September.","You can ___ at eighteen and continue learning at college.","To earn money this summer, I hope to ___ at a café.","I would like to ___ somewhere with space to play outdoors.","After forty years at the museum, he plans to ___ next spring."],"extendedDialog":[["Maya","Did you find anything for the museum display?"],["Theo","Yes. My aunt gave me a record player from the nineteen eighties."],["Maya","Does it still work?"],["Theo","It does, but we need a cable. I'll bring it on Thursday, not Tuesday."],["Maya","Great. I'm writing the display labels. What did people use it for at your aunt's house?"],["Theo","She used to play one record every Sunday while the family prepared lunch. They had a radio too, but she liked choosing exactly what to hear."],["Maya","Could she take it on holiday, like we take our phones?"],["Theo","Not really. It was heavy and needed electricity. She took a little battery radio to the beach instead. I have a photograph of both objects in the same room."],["Maya","Let's put the photograph next to the player. Some visitors may have never seen an old cable or a record, so we'll explain the difference."]],"extendedListening":[["What are the speakers preparing?","A museum display about older technology.","A family holiday.","A sale of modern phones."],["What did Theo find?","A record player.","A radio.","A typewriter."],["When will he bring it?","Thursday.","Tuesday.","Friday."],["Why did Theo's aunt prefer records at home?","She could choose the music herself.","The records worked without electricity.","Her radio was broken."],["What did she take to the beach?","A small radio.","The record player.","A photograph of the player."],["Why include the old photograph?","To show the objects in their original setting.","To advertise a new record.","To replace the display label."]],"dialogueWords":145,"readingLesson":{"title":"A street in two time periods","paragraphs":["When Rosa helped to clear an old room, she found a small camera and a box of photos. Her grandfather explained that he used to take photographs on family trips. The camera could only take a limited number of pictures before he needed a new roll of film. Rosa noticed that some photos showed a tram outside her house. Today there is no tram on the street, but the old stop is still there. She compared the pictures with a modern map for a school project.","Rosa wanted to find out when the tram stopped running. The date was not on the back of the photos, so she carried one to the local library. A librarian showed her an old **timetable**. It listed the street as part of Route 3, but it did not say when the route closed. An article in a local newspaper gave her the missing **detail**: the final tram had run in October, many years before she was born.","Next, Rosa took a new photo from the same **angle**. An older shop had become a café, and a tree now stood where passengers had once waited. She chose one **similarity** as well: the entrance to her building still had the same stone steps. At the end of her **presentation**, she invited her classmates to bring their own old pictures. Two pupils discovered that their families had lived in the same street at different times."],"trueFalse":[["F","The date of the last tram was written on a photograph.","A newspaper article gave the missing information."],["T","The street used to be part of Route 3.","The timetable listed it on that route."],["F","Rosa photographed the street from a different angle.","She took the new photo from the same angle."],["T","The stone steps looked the same in both photos.","The entrance still had the same steps."]],"gaps":[["At the library Rosa looked at an old ___.",["timetable"]],["The old shop has become a ___.",["cafe","café"]],["The final tram ran in ___.",["october"]]],"definitions":[["timetable","a list of times when a transport service runs"],["detail","one small piece of information"],["angle","the direction or position from which you see something"],["similarity","a way in which two things are alike"],["presentation","a talk showing information to a group"]]}},{"title":"Goals","topic":"Цели, достижения и семьи слов","page":36,"words":[["win a competition","выиграть соревнование"],["get good grades","получать хорошие оценки"],["make progress","добиваться прогресса"],["achieve a goal","достичь цели"],["feel proud","гордиться"],["give up","сдаться"],["achieve","достигать"],["achievement","достижение"],["improve","улучшать"],["improvement","улучшение"],["decide","решать"],["decision","решение"]],"grammar":[{"title":"Past continuous","rule":"Was или were + -ing описывает действие, которое шло в определённый момент в прошлом.","items":[["At six I ___ for the race.","was training","trained,were training"],["They ___ a plan when I arrived.","were making","was making,are making"],["What ___ you doing at eight?","were","was,did"],["Mia ___ listening at that moment.","wasn't","weren't,didn't"]]},{"title":"Past simple и continuous с when / while","rule":"Длительный фон — past continuous. Короткое событие, которое произошло на его фоне, — past simple.","items":[["I was practising when my friend ___.","called","was calling every day,call"],["While she ___, the lights went out.","was studying","studies,were studying"],["We were waiting when the bus ___.","arrived","arrives,were arriving"],["While they ___, I took a photo.","were playing","plays,was playing"]]}],"text":"Liam wanted to run five kilometres without stopping. At first he tried to run every day, but he soon felt tired. His cousin helped him make a better plan. He ran three times a week and wrote his times in a diary. One morning, while he was training in the park, it began to rain. He wanted to stop but decided to finish the route slowly. Six weeks later he finished his first five-kilometre run. The time was not important to him. Keeping his promise was.","reading":[["What changed after his cousin helped?","He trained three times a week.","He stopped using a diary.","He ran every day."],["What mattered most to Liam?","Keeping his promise.","Getting the fastest time.","Winning a medal."]],"dialog":[["Maya","What were you doing when I texted last night?"],["Theo","I was practising my speech for the competition."],["Maya","What's your goal?"],["Theo","I want to speak for three minutes without reading my notes."]],"listening":[["What was Theo doing?","Practising a speech.","Training for a race.","Writing a diary."],["What is his goal?","To speak for three minutes without notes.","To learn six words.","To finish in two minutes."]],"speaking":"Tell a partner about a goal you set. Explain what helped you make progress.","writing":"Write an entry for a goal diary. Set a goal, give two milestones and describe one difficulty you could face.","contexts":["If your entry is judged the best, you will ___.","If I revise a little every day, I hope to ___.","Keep a diary of your practice so you can see whether you ___.","Set a clear target and choose one action that will help you ___.","You can ___ of finishing even if you come last.","When the task gets difficult, take a break rather than ___.","If you practise regularly, you can ___ something that seemed impossible at first.","Finishing my first race was a real ___.","I record my speeches because I want to ___ my delivery.","The last version is clearer. That's a big ___.","Our group must ___ which project to enter by Friday.","After hearing both suggestions, we made a ___."],"extendedDialog":[["Maya","What were you doing when I texted last night?"],["Theo","I was practising my speech for the competition."],["Maya","What's your goal?"],["Theo","I want to speak for three minutes without reading my notes."],["Maya","Have you tried saying it in front of someone? There is a difference between getting through the speech and making people want to listen."],["Theo","I did it for my sister. She said the first part was clear, but I looked at the floor when I explained my main idea. I didn't realise I was doing that."],["Maya","Try recording yourself. Then choose one thing to change, not everything at once."],["Theo","I'll mark a short pause before the main idea. My first practice took four minutes. Last night it was three minutes and twenty seconds, so I still need to cut a little."]],"extendedListening":[["What skill are they discussing?","Preparing and improving a speech.","Running a race faster.","Making a goal diary app."],["What was Theo doing?","Practising a speech.","Training for a race.","Writing a diary."],["What is his goal?","To speak for three minutes without notes.","To learn six words.","To finish in two minutes."],["What did Theo's sister notice?","He looked at the floor during the main idea.","He spoke too quietly at the start.","He never read from his notes."],["What does Maya advise him to do?","Record himself and change one thing at a time.","Practise without ever taking a break.","Add two more examples."],["How long was his latest practice?","Three minutes and twenty seconds.","Exactly three minutes.","Four minutes."]],"dialogueWords":132,"readingLesson":{"title":"The goal diary","paragraphs":["Liam wanted to run five kilometres without stopping. At first he tried to run every day, but he soon felt tired. His cousin helped him make a better plan. He ran three times a week and wrote his times in a diary. One morning, while he was training in the park, it began to rain. He wanted to stop but decided to finish the route slowly. Six weeks later he finished his first five-kilometre run. The time was not important to him. Keeping his promise was.","After the run, Liam opened his diary to see which weeks had gone well. Three entries surprised him. His time had not improved when he ran farther every day. Instead, he made the most **progress** in weeks when he also took rest days. His cousin suggested recording how he felt as well as how fast he ran. Liam added a simple **scale** from one to five and began giving each session a number.","Soon the diary helped with something besides running. Liam wanted to improve his French listening, so he set a new **target**: five minutes of practice on four days each week. He put a mark beside each day he finished. On Friday he listened to Monday’s recording again and noticed that he understood two more words. At the end of the month, he shared his **method** with a friend who was learning guitar. They agreed to **compare** their notes every Sunday and change anything that did not help."],"trueFalse":[["F","Liam improved most when he ran farther every day.","His best weeks also included rest days."],["T","He added a scale from one to five.","He used the scale to record how each session felt."],["F","His French plan was to study for an hour every day.","He planned five minutes on four days a week."],["T","The friend Liam shared his method with was learning guitar.","They planned to compare their practice notes."]],"gaps":[["Liam decided to record both his speed and how he ___.",["felt"]],["His French practice target was ___ minutes at a time.",["five","5"]],["The two friends agreed to compare notes every ___.",["sunday"]]],"definitions":[["progress","movement towards a better result"],["scale","a set of numbers used for measuring something"],["target","a result you aim to reach"],["method","a way of doing something"],["compare","to look for ways in which two things are alike or different"]]}},{"title":"Spend!","topic":"Деньги, покупки и сравнение","page":48,"words":[["price","цена"],["discount","скидка"],["receipt","чек"],["cash","наличные"],["change","сдача"],["budget","бюджет"],["cheaply","дёшево"],["carefully","внимательно"],["quickly","быстро"],["politely","вежливо"],["save up","копить"],["second-hand","подержанный"]],"grammar":[{"title":"Quantifiers","rule":"Many — с исчисляемыми, much — с неисчисляемыми. Enough означает, что количества достаточно.","items":[["We haven't got ___ money for both books.","enough","many,a few"],["There aren't ___ tickets left.","many","much,any of money"],["Do you have ___ cash?","any","many,a few"],["There are too ___ people in this shop.","many","much,enough of"]]},{"title":"Сравнение","rule":"У коротких прилагательных чаще -er/-est. У длинных — more/most. As … as показывает равенство.","items":[["This game is ___ than that one.","cheaper","cheapest,cheap"],["It's the ___ expensive bag in the shop.","most","more,much"],["The blue one isn't as heavy ___ the red one.","as","than,like"],["This is ___ value than the other offer.","better","best,good"]]}],"text":"Ada wanted to buy a second-hand jacket. One seller asked for twelve pounds, but the jacket needed a new zip. Another jacket cost sixteen pounds and was ready to wear. At first Ada thought the cheaper one was the best deal. Then she checked the repair cost: seven pounds. She decided to buy the second jacket and asked for a receipt. The experience taught her to compare the total cost rather than just the price on the label.","reading":[["Which jacket did Ada buy?","The one that cost £16.","The one that cost £12.","Both jackets."],["Why wasn't the cheapest label the best deal?","The repair made it cost more overall.","It had no discount label.","Ada had no cash."]],"dialog":[["Maya","I've got twenty pounds. Is that enough for the backpack?"],["Theo","The large one is twenty-two, but the small one is sixteen."],["Maya","Is the small one as strong as the large one?"],["Theo","Yes. There is no difference in the material."]],"listening":[["Which bag fits the budget?","The small backpack.","The large backpack.","Neither backpack."],["How much does the small one cost?","£16.","£20.","£22."]],"speaking":"Role-play a purchase. Ask about a discount, compare two choices and make a decision.","writing":"Write a listing for a second-hand item. Describe it, set a fair price and explain why it is good value.","contexts":["Before you pay, check the ___ on the label.","I received a ten percent ___ because the box was damaged.","Keep the ___ in case you need to return the jacket.","The stall can't take cards, so bring some ___.","I gave the seller ten pounds and received three pounds in ___.","Our group has a forty-pound ___ to spend on the party.","If we borrow the tools, we can make the shelves ___.","Read the measurements ___ before you order the desk.","The shop closes in two minutes, so choose ___.","Even if you're unhappy with the service, explain the problem ___.","I'm going to ___ for a camera instead of using all my money now.","A ___ coat has already belonged to someone else."],"extendedDialog":[["Maya","I've got twenty pounds. Is that enough for the backpack?"],["Theo","The large one is twenty-two, but the small one is sixteen."],["Maya","Is the small one as strong as the large one?"],["Theo","Yes. There is no difference in the material."],["Maya","I need it for school, but I also want space for my trainers. The small bag looks fine, although the zip doesn't move very smoothly."],["Theo","You can try this green one instead. It is the same size and price, and has a separate pocket. If you are still unsure, compare it with the one on that shelf."],["Maya","The other shop has a similar bag for fourteen, but they charge four pounds for delivery. This one is better value if I take it with me today."],["Theo","Good. Keep the receipt. You have thirty days to bring it back if you haven't used it."]],"extendedListening":[["What is Maya comparing?","The total cost and usefulness of different bags.","Two different delivery companies.","Prices for trainers."],["Which bag fits the budget?","The small backpack.","The large backpack.","Neither backpack."],["How much does the small one cost?","£16.","£20.","£22."],["Why does she consider the green bag?","It has a separate pocket and costs the same as the small one.","It is bigger than the large bag.","It includes a free pair of trainers."],["How much would the other shop charge including delivery?","£18.","£14.","£16."],["Why should Maya keep the receipt?","She may need it if she returns the bag.","It gives her a free delivery code.","It tells her how to fix the zip."]],"dialogueWords":141,"readingLesson":{"title":"Is it really cheaper?","paragraphs":["Ada wanted to buy a second-hand jacket. One seller asked for twelve pounds, but the jacket needed a new zip. Another jacket cost sixteen pounds and was ready to wear. At first Ada thought the cheaper one was the best deal. Then she checked the repair cost: seven pounds. She decided to buy the second jacket and asked for a receipt. The experience taught her to compare the total cost rather than just the price on the label.","The following Saturday, Ada helped at a second-hand market. The organisers gave each helper a twenty-pound **budget** to choose objects for a classroom display. Ada liked a lamp that cost eight pounds, but the seller said its cable was broken. A teacher could repair it, although the **repair** would cost six pounds for parts. A working lamp on the next table cost twelve pounds. Ada wrote both totals on a small chart before making a **decision**.","Her partner suggested spending the remaining money on frames. They found two frames for three pounds each, which left two pounds for labels. At the end of the morning they asked for a **receipt** for the lamp, because the school needed proof of the purchase. Back in class, Ada explained why the first price is only one part of a purchase. A good **deal** also depends on whether you can use the item immediately and what else you will have to pay for."],"trueFalse":[["T","Each helper had twenty pounds to spend.","That was the budget for the classroom display."],["F","The broken lamp cost twelve pounds before repairs.","It cost eight pounds before repairs."],["T","The two frames cost six pounds in total.","Each frame cost three pounds."],["F","The school did not need proof of the purchase.","Ada asked for a receipt for that reason."]],"gaps":[["The total cost of the broken lamp and the parts would be £___.",["14","fourteen"]],["After choosing the frames they had £___ left for labels.",["2","two"]],["Ada asked for a ___ as proof of the purchase.",["receipt"]]],"definitions":[["budget","the amount of money available to spend"],["repair","work that makes a broken object usable again"],["decision","a choice made after thinking about options"],["receipt","a record showing that you paid for something"],["deal","an agreement to buy something at a particular price"]]}},{"title":"A better place","topic":"Дом, мебель и окружающая среда","page":60,"words":[["shelf","полка"],["wardrobe","шкаф"],["sofa","диван"],["desk","письменный стол"],["balcony","балкон"],["armchair","кресло"],["recycle","перерабатывать"],["save energy","экономить энергию"],["waste","отходы"],["pollution","загрязнение"],["reusable","многоразовый"],["public transport","общественный транспорт"]],"grammar":[{"title":"Will и might","rule":"Will выражает прогноз, а might — менее уверенную возможность. После обоих глагол без to.","items":[["I think homes ___ use less energy in the future.","will","are,will to"],["It ___ rain later, so take a jacket.","might","does to,might to"],["I'm sure this room ___ look better with plants.","will","can to,does to"],["Solar panels might ___ us money.","save","saves,saving"]]},{"title":"First и zero conditional","rule":"Zero описывает закономерность: present + present. First — возможный будущий результат: present + will.","items":[["If you heat ice, it ___.","melts","will to melt,melt"],["If we recycle more, we ___ less waste next year.","will produce","produced,will to produce"],["If she ___ the light off, we will save energy.","turns","will turn,turn"],["Plants die if they ___ enough water.","don't get","won't gets,doesn't get"]]}],"text":"A group of students looked at an empty space outside their school. Some wanted a garden. Others wanted a place to sit between classes. They drew a plan that included both ideas and chose plants that need very little water. Old wooden boxes became seats and plant containers. At first everyone worried about the cost, but a local shop donated the wood. The students think the space will be ready in May. If it rains a lot, the opening might be later.","reading":[["What did the plan include?","A garden and a place to sit.","Only a garden.","A car park and a shop."],["Why might the opening be later?","It might rain a lot.","There is no wood.","Nobody chose plants."]],"dialog":[["Maya","If we put the desk near the window, we'll need the light less often."],["Theo","Good idea. I think we might move the sofa as well."],["Maya","Where will it go?"],["Theo","Next to the shelf, so there's more space near the door."]],"listening":[["Where will they put the desk?","Near the window.","Next to the door.","Behind the sofa."],["Why may they move the sofa?","To make more space near the door.","To put it outside.","To sell it."]],"speaking":"Suggest two changes to make your room or school more useful and greener.","writing":"Write a proposal for a greener classroom. Include one prediction and two if-sentences.","contexts":["Put the dictionaries on the top ___.","I hang my jackets inside the ___.","Three people can sit on the ___ by the TV.","I do my homework at the ___ by the window.","You can step outside onto the ___ and water the plants.","Dad likes reading in the ___ because it has a high back and armrests.","At school we ___ paper in the blue bin.","Turn lights off when you leave to ___.","Buying only the food we need cuts down on ___.","Heavy traffic can increase air ___ near schools.","Take a ___ bottle and refill it during the day.","The bus and train are forms of ___."],"extendedDialog":[["Maya","If we put the desk near the window, we'll need the light less often."],["Theo","Good idea. I think we might move the sofa as well."],["Maya","Where will it go?"],["Theo","Next to the shelf, so there's more space near the door."],["Maya","We also have four old wooden boxes from the storeroom. We could use them as plant containers instead of buying new ones."],["Theo","Let's measure the space. If we put them too close to the door, people won't be able to walk past easily. The balcony is wider, but it gets strong sun in the afternoon."],["Maya","We could choose plants that don't need much water. Would you put the recycling bin near the balcony as well?"],["Theo","I'd keep the bin by the entrance. More people will use it if they see it on the way out. Then we'll have enough space for two or three boxes outside."]],"extendedListening":[["What are the speakers trying to do?","Make a room more useful and environmentally friendly.","Buy new furniture for a shop.","Organise a party on the balcony."],["Where will they put the desk?","Near the window.","Next to the door.","Behind the sofa."],["Why may they move the sofa?","To make more space near the door.","To put it outside.","To sell it."],["Why might the boxes be a problem near the door?","They could block the way.","They could get too much sun.","They would be too easy to see."],["What sort of plants does Maya suggest?","Plants that need little water.","Plants that only grow at night.","Plants that need new pots every week."],["Why put the bin by the entrance?","More people will notice and use it.","It has to stay out of sunlight.","It is too heavy to carry outside."]],"dialogueWords":146,"readingLesson":{"title":"A space for more than one idea","paragraphs":["A group of students looked at an empty space outside their school. Some wanted a garden. Others wanted a place to sit between classes. They drew a plan that included both ideas and chose plants that need very little water. Old wooden boxes became seats and plant containers. At first everyone worried about the cost, but a local shop donated the wood. The students think the space will be ready in May. If it rains a lot, the opening might be later.","Before opening the garden, the students watched how people used the path outside their school. At lunch it became busy, so they moved the flower boxes back to leave a wider **entrance**. They also put two seats in the shade. A pupil who used a wheelchair tried the new layout and explained that one of the tables needed more space underneath. The group made the **adjustment** the same afternoon.","The next problem was watering. In the holidays, the school building would be closed and nobody wanted to leave a tap running. A science teacher helped the group collect rain in a covered **container**. Students made a list of plants that needed little water and added a small **sign** asking visitors to leave the plants where they found them. When the garden opened, people stayed there during breaks and lessons sometimes moved outside. The group planned to ask for **feedback** in June, after everyone had had time to try the space."],"trueFalse":[["T","The path became busy at lunch.","The students watched it before opening the garden."],["F","The group ignored a pupil’s suggestion about a table.","They adjusted the table that afternoon."],["F","The students planned to leave a tap running in the holidays.","They chose to collect rain instead."],["T","They planned to ask for feedback in June.","They wanted visitors to have time to try the space first."]],"gaps":[["The students moved the boxes to leave a wider ___.",["entrance"]],["The science teacher helped them collect ___.",["rain","rainwater","rain water"]],["The students planned to ask for feedback in ___.",["june"]]],"definitions":[["entrance","a place where people enter a space"],["adjustment","a small change made to improve something"],["container","an object that can hold something"],["sign","a notice with a message or instruction"],["feedback","information about what worked and what could improve"]]}},{"title":"Experience","topic":"Жизненный опыт и музыка","page":72,"words":[["enter a competition","участвовать в конкурсе"],["try a new sport","попробовать новый спорт"],["perform on stage","выступать на сцене"],["meet a celebrity","встретить знаменитость"],["travel abroad","путешествовать за границу"],["volunteer","работать волонтёром"],["band","группа"],["drummer","барабанщик"],["gig","концерт"],["audience","публика"],["lyrics","текст песни"],["rehearse","репетировать"]],"grammar":[{"title":"Present perfect: утверждения и отрицания","rule":"Have/has + past participle связывает прошлый опыт с настоящим; время события не уточняется.","items":[["I ___ performed on stage twice.","have","am,did"],["Mia ___ heard this band before.","hasn't","didn't has,haven't"],["They have ___ a music competition.","entered","enter,entering"],["Leo has ___ abroad several times.","travelled","travel,travelling"]]},{"title":"Present perfect: вопросы, ever и never","rule":"Have/has ставим перед подлежащим. Ever — когда-либо, never — никогда; never уже выражает отрицание.","items":[["___ you ever tried a new sport?","Have","Did,Are"],["Has Mia ever ___ on stage?","sung","sang,sing"],["I've ___ met a celebrity.","never","not never,ever never"],["Have they ever ___ this song?","played","play,playing"]]}],"text":"Niko loved music but had never performed in public. When the youth centre asked for volunteers for an open night, he signed up to help with sound. During a rehearsal a drummer was absent, so Niko offered to play one song. The others said he was ready for the concert too. He has now played several small gigs. He still gets nervous before each one, but he has learned to focus on the first few notes and breathe slowly.","reading":[["Why did Niko originally sign up?","To help with sound.","To perform a solo.","To meet a celebrity."],["What helps Niko now?","Focusing on the first notes.","Avoiding rehearsals.","Playing faster."]],"dialog":[["Maya","Have you ever sung in front of an audience?"],["Theo","No, but I've played the drums at two school concerts."],["Maya","Would you like to try singing at our club?"],["Theo","Maybe. Can I come to a rehearsal first?"]],"listening":[["What has Theo done twice?","Played at school concerts.","Sung at the club.","Written lyrics."],["What does he want to do first?","Attend a rehearsal.","Buy a drum kit.","Lead the concert."]],"speaking":"Interview someone about two experiences. Ask a follow-up question about one of them.","writing":"Write a profile of someone who has tried a new activity. Give a reason for trying it and explain what changed.","contexts":["Would you like to ___? You could send in a short story.","Our club invites beginners to ___ each month.","The drama group will ___ in front of their families.","The winner will get to ___ from the world of film.","My brother wants to ___ and improve his Spanish.","You can ___ at the library without being paid.","Four students play together in a ___.","The ___ practised the rhythm before the other musicians arrived.","We're playing a ___ in a small club on Saturday.","The ___ applauded at the end of the performance.","I like the melody, but I can't understand the ___.","We need to ___ before we play for the audience."],"extendedDialog":[["Maya","Have you ever sung in front of an audience?"],["Theo","No, but I've played the drums at two school concerts."],["Maya","Would you like to try singing at our club?"],["Theo","Maybe. Can I come to a rehearsal first?"],["Maya","Of course. We're rehearsing in the small hall on Tuesday. At first you can join two other singers, so you don't have to do a solo."],["Theo","That's a relief. I don't mind an audience when I'm behind the drums, but everyone can hear a voice clearly. Have any of the other singers performed before?"],["Maya","One of them has sung on stage, but the other is new too. We usually record the last practice and listen back. It often sounds much better than it felt."],["Theo","All right, I'll try. If singing isn't for me, I can still help with the drums at the gig."]],"extendedListening":[["What is Theo considering?","Trying a new role in a music group.","Leaving the music club entirely.","Buying a new drum kit."],["What has Theo done twice?","Played at school concerts.","Sung at the club.","Written lyrics."],["What does he want to do first?","Attend a rehearsal.","Buy a drum kit.","Lead the concert."],["How will he start singing?","With two other singers.","Alone in front of the audience.","Only by recording at home."],["Why do they record the last practice?","To hear how the performance actually sounds.","To replace the live concert.","To learn the lyrics from a website."],["What could Theo do if he decides against singing?","Play the drums at the gig.","Cancel rehearsal for everyone.","Sell tickets at a shop."]],"dialogueWords":139,"readingLesson":{"title":"Niko’s first gig","paragraphs":["Niko loved music but had never performed in public. When the youth centre asked for volunteers for an open night, he signed up to help with sound. During a rehearsal a drummer was absent, so Niko offered to play one song. The others said he was ready for the concert too. He has now played several small gigs. He still gets nervous before each one, but he has learned to focus on the first few notes and breathe slowly.","At Niko’s first public **performance**, the group arrived early to check the microphones. The sound in the hall was different from the sound at rehearsal. Niko could hear the singer clearly but could hardly hear the guitar. Their **sound engineer** moved one speaker closer to the musicians. Then the group played only the first part of each song to check levels and save time.","Just before they went on, a guitarist’s string broke. Niko expected the group to wait, but the singer invited him to play a short drum **solo** while the guitarist fitted a new string. Niko took a breath, started with a rhythm he knew well and changed it a little each time. A few people in the **crowd** began to clap to the beat. Later the guitarist thanked him for helping. Niko wrote about the evening in his diary. His biggest **achievement** was staying calm when something unexpected happened."],"trueFalse":[["T","The group checked the microphones before the performance.","They arrived early to do a sound check."],["F","Niko could hear the guitar better than the singer.","He could hardly hear the guitar."],["T","Niko played while the guitarist changed a string.","The singer invited him to fill the short gap."],["F","Niko felt the most important achievement was playing faster.","His achievement was staying calm."]],"gaps":[["The sound engineer moved a ___ closer to the musicians.",["speaker"]],["The singer asked Niko to play a drum ___.",["solo"]],["Some people in the crowd began to ___ to the beat.",["clap"]]],"definitions":[["performance","an occasion when people play or act for others"],["sound engineer","a person who controls how music or speech sounds"],["solo","a piece performed by one person on their own"],["crowd","a large group of people in one place"],["achievement","something you succeed in doing after making an effort"]]}},{"title":"My stuff","topic":"Описание вещей и их история","page":84,"words":[["plain","однотонный"],["striped","полосатый"],["wooden","деревянный"],["leather","кожаный"],["round","круглый"],["handmade","сделанный вручную"],["useful","полезный"],["careless","небрежный"],["colourful","яркий"],["washable","пригодный для стирки"],["comfortable","удобный"],["valuable","ценный"]],"grammar":[{"title":"Present perfect: for и since","rule":"For — период, since — начальная точка. Present perfect связывает начавшуюся в прошлом ситуацию с настоящим.","items":[["I've had this bag ___ three years.","for","since,ago"],["She's kept the photo ___ 2021.","since","for,during"],["How long ___ you had it?","have","did,are"],["We ___ owned this table since June.","have","did,are"]]},{"title":"Present perfect и past simple","rule":"Для завершённого времени (last year, yesterday) используем past simple. Для опыта или связи с настоящим — present perfect.","items":[["I ___ this camera last year.","bought","have bought,buy"],["I ___ three photos today and might take more.","have taken","took yesterday,take yesterday"],["She ___ the jacket two weeks ago.","found","has found,finds"],["I ___ never lost my keys.","have","did,am"]]}],"text":"Mira has kept a wooden pencil box since primary school. It came from her older cousin, who painted tiny stars on the lid. The box is too small for many school supplies, but Mira still uses it to keep letters and concert tickets. Last year she repaired the hinge instead of replacing it. She says the box has become more important over time because it reminds her of people and events that she might otherwise forget.","reading":[["How did Mira get the box?","It came from her cousin.","She won it at a concert.","She bought it online."],["What did she do last year?","She repaired the hinge.","She replaced the box.","She painted it blue."]],"dialog":[["Maya","How long have you had that leather bag?"],["Theo","Since my thirteenth birthday. My uncle bought it for me."],["Maya","Is it still useful?"],["Theo","Yes. I replaced the strap last month, so I can still take it to school."]],"listening":[["Who gave Theo the bag?","His uncle.","His teacher.","His sister."],["What did Theo replace?","The strap.","The zip.","The bag."]],"speaking":"Describe a possession you have kept for a long time. Explain why it matters to you.","writing":"Write a catalogue entry for an exhibition of meaningful objects. Include how long you have had yours and how you got it.","contexts":["The shirt is ___ blue with no pattern.","He wore a ___ scarf with red and white lines.","The ___ box is made from oak.","The ___ strap is made from animal hide.","The table is ___, so there is no corner to bump into.","The card is ___; my friend made it herself.","The extra pocket is ___ when I need to carry my keys.","It was ___ to leave the camera outside overnight.","The poster will be more ___ if we add some bright red and blue.","Check whether the cover is ___ before you put it in the washing machine.","These shoes are ___ enough to wear all day.","This watch is ___ because it belonged to my great-grandmother."],"extendedDialog":[["Maya","How long have you had that leather bag?"],["Theo","Since my thirteenth birthday. My uncle bought it for me."],["Maya","Is it still useful?"],["Theo","Yes. I replaced the strap last month, so I can still take it to school."],["Maya","We're planning an exhibition of objects with a story. Would you lend it to us for a week?"],["Theo","Maybe, if it's safe. It's plain brown, so it won't stand out in a display of bright new things. But I've carried it on almost every school trip since I got it."],["Maya","That's precisely why it belongs in the exhibition. Could you bring a photo of one of those trips? We can put it next to the bag with a label about the repair."],["Theo","I'll look for a photo from last spring. I can leave the bag with you on Monday, but I'll need it back by Friday afternoon."]],"extendedListening":[["Why does Maya want the bag?","It tells a personal story for an exhibition.","She wants to buy it for a trip.","She needs it to repair another bag."],["Who gave Theo the bag?","His uncle.","His teacher.","His sister."],["What did Theo replace?","The strap.","The zip.","The bag."],["What does Theo think might make the bag less noticeable?","It is plain brown.","It has no strap.","It is too large for the room."],["What will sit next to the bag?","A photo and a label about the repair.","A pair of shoes.","A new leather bag."],["By when does Theo need it back?","Friday afternoon.","Monday morning.","Next spring."]],"dialogueWords":144,"readingLesson":{"title":"The objects we keep","paragraphs":["Mira has kept a wooden pencil box since primary school. It came from her older cousin, who painted tiny stars on the lid. The box is too small for many school supplies, but Mira still uses it to keep letters and concert tickets. Last year she repaired the hinge instead of replacing it. She says the box has become more important over time because it reminds her of people and events that she might otherwise forget.","Mira showed her pencil box to an older neighbour who makes furniture. He explained that the metal **hinge** had become loose because the wood around it was soft. Instead of using a larger screw, he filled the old hole with a tiny piece of wood. It took five minutes, and the lid could open smoothly again. Mira decided to make a short video of the **process** so she could remember it.","Her school was preparing a display about personal **possessions**, and Mira brought the box and two of the concert tickets inside it. A classmate brought a scarf that had been made by his aunt. Another brought a small shell from a beach he had visited with his brother. Each person wrote a **label** explaining why the item mattered. The display was successful because every **object** told a different story, even though none of them had cost much. At the end, several visitors asked to add their own objects."],"trueFalse":[["F","Mira’s neighbour used a larger screw to fix the lid.","He filled the old hole with a small piece of wood."],["T","Mira made a video so she could remember the repair.","The video recorded the process."],["F","Mira’s classmate bought his scarf at the exhibition.","His aunt had made it."],["T","Visitors wanted to contribute their own objects.","Several asked about adding them."]],"gaps":[["The repair took about ___ minutes.",["five","5"]],["Mira brought two concert ___ to the display.",["tickets"]],["One classmate brought a small ___ from a beach.",["shell"]]],"definitions":[["hinge","a moving part that lets a door or lid open"],["process","a series of steps used to do something"],["possessions","things that someone owns"],["label","a short written description put next to an item"],["object","a thing you can see or touch"]]}},{"title":"Responsibility","topic":"Домашние дела и планы","page":96,"words":[["do the washing-up","мыть посуду"],["take out the rubbish","выносить мусор"],["vacuum the floor","пылесосить"],["feed the pet","кормить питомца"],["tidy my room","убирать комнату"],["set the table","накрывать на стол"],["tiring","утомительный"],["tired","уставший"],["boring","скучный"],["bored","скучающий"],["relaxing","расслабляющий"],["relaxed","расслабленный"]],"grammar":[{"title":"Have to","rule":"Have to — обязанность. Don’t have to — отсутствие необходимости. С he/she употребляем has to.","items":[["Mia ___ feed the cat every morning.","has to","have to,has"],["We ___ wash up today because the dishwasher is on.","don't have to","doesn't have to,have don't"],["Do you ___ set the table?","have to","has to,having to"],["Theo ___ take the rubbish out today because it's not his turn.","doesn't have to","don't have to,doesn't has to"]]},{"title":"Will и going to","rule":"Going to — запланированное намерение. Will часто используем для решения в момент разговора.","items":[["I've already made a plan. I ___ tidy my room after lunch.","am going to","go to,was going"],["That bag looks heavy. I ___ carry it for you.","will","am,going to"],["What are you ___ do tomorrow?","going to","will,go to"],["We agreed yesterday that we ___ make a rota.","are going to","will to,going"]]}],"text":"In Sam's house everyone helped, but no one knew who was doing which job. One evening the rubbish was still in the kitchen and the dog had not been fed. Sam suggested making a simple weekly rota. Each person chose a job they did not mind doing, and they agreed to swap the least popular chores each week. After a month the family realised that the rota had saved both time and arguments. They are going to add gardening to it in spring.","reading":[["Why did the family create a rota?","They often forgot who was doing each job.","They wanted to buy a dog.","They had no chores."],["What will they add in spring?","Gardening.","Cooking breakfast.","A second pet."]],"dialog":[["Maya","I've already made my list. I'm going to vacuum and then feed the dog."],["Theo","Do you have to take the rubbish out as well?"],["Maya","No, it's Leo's turn. But the dog's water bowl is empty."],["Theo","I'll fill it now."]],"listening":[["Which job belongs to Leo?","Taking the rubbish out.","Vacuuming.","Feeding the dog."],["What does Theo offer to do?","Fill the water bowl.","Wash the dishes.","Make the list."]],"speaking":"Negotiate a fair plan for three chores. Explain which jobs you have to do and when.","writing":"Write a household rota for three people. Include what each person has to do, one plan and one offer of help.","contexts":["After dinner I'll ___ and put the plates away.","Remember to ___ before the bin lorry comes.","Could you ___? There are crumbs all over the carpet.","We have to ___ before we leave for school.","I need to ___ because my books are all over the floor.","Please ___ for four people. The plates are in the cupboard.","Carrying the furniture up the stairs was ___.","I'm too ___ to finish the last job tonight.","We stopped watching the film because it was ___.","If you're ___, ask if you can choose a different activity.","I find gardening ___ after a difficult day.","After a quiet walk, I felt much more ___."],"extendedDialog":[["Maya","I've already made my list. I'm going to vacuum and then feed the dog."],["Theo","Do you have to take the rubbish out as well?"],["Maya","No, it's Leo's turn. But the dog's water bowl is empty."],["Theo","I'll fill it now."],["Maya","Thanks. Last week everyone thought somebody else was looking after the dog, so we made a family rota."],["Theo","Does the rota tell you what to do when someone can't do their jobs?"],["Maya","Yes, we have to ask to swap before dinner. On Wednesday I have basketball practice, so I'm going to set the table on Thursday instead. Leo will do it on Wednesday."],["Theo","That's fair. At home I usually do the washing-up, but tomorrow my sister is going to do it because I'm helping her with a school project later."]],"extendedListening":[["What are they discussing?","How to share and swap household jobs.","How to train a dog.","Where to play basketball."],["Which job belongs to Leo?","Taking the rubbish out.","Vacuuming.","Feeding the dog."],["What does Theo offer to do?","Fill the water bowl.","Wash the dishes.","Make the list."],["What should someone do before dinner?","Ask to swap a job if necessary.","Feed the dog twice.","Write a school report."],["Why is Maya swapping days?","She has basketball practice on Wednesday.","She is visiting Theo on Thursday.","She doesn't know how to set the table."],["Why will Theo's sister do the washing-up tomorrow?","Theo will help her with a project later.","Theo never does that job.","She has decided to cook dinner."]],"dialogueWords":129,"readingLesson":{"title":"Making a rota fair","paragraphs":["In Sam's house everyone helped, but no one knew who was doing which job. One evening the rubbish was still in the kitchen and the dog had not been fed. Sam suggested making a simple weekly rota. Each person chose a job they did not mind doing, and they agreed to swap the least popular chores each week. After a month the family realised that the rota had saved both time and arguments. They are going to add gardening to it in spring.","The family’s first rota looked fair because each person had the same number of chores. Then Sam noticed that some jobs took much longer than others. Feeding the dog took only a few minutes, while cleaning the kitchen took nearly half an hour. He suggested adding an **estimate** of the time next to each task. The family compared the totals and made a few changes to the **schedule**.","They also agreed on what to do when plans changed. If someone could not finish a task, they had to **swap** it with another person before dinner. If no one could help that day, the family could move a less **urgent** job to the weekend. Nobody wanted the dog to wait for food, but the windows could be cleaned later. At the end of the month, they asked whether the new system made everyone’s **workload** more equal. The children said they knew what to do more often, and the adults said they spent less time reminding people."],"trueFalse":[["T","At first everyone had the same number of jobs.","The first rota counted tasks rather than minutes."],["F","All jobs took about the same amount of time.","Cleaning the kitchen took much longer than feeding the dog."],["T","People had to arrange swaps before dinner.","That was the family’s rule for changes."],["F","The family thought that feeding the dog could wait until the weekend.","They considered feeding the dog urgent."]],"gaps":[["Sam suggested adding an estimate of the ___ each task took.",["time"]],["They agreed that windows could be cleaned at the ___.",["weekend"]],["The adults said they spent less time ___ people.",["reminding"]]],"definitions":[["estimate","an approximate idea of an amount"],["schedule","a plan that says what happens and when"],["swap","to exchange one thing or task for another"],["urgent","needing to be dealt with soon"],["workload","the total amount of work someone has to do"]]}}]};
